            "value": "<div data-page-id=\"YP3XdinBZozo9Qx3V4elcqv1gBd\" data-lark-html-role=\"root\" data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\">\n<div class=\"ace-line ace-line old-record-id-OuphdyB66oaXaexoKD4lLtSvgnh\">\n<div data-page-id=\"YP3XdinBZozo9Qx3V4elcqv1gBd\" data-lark-html-role=\"root\" data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\">\n<div class=\"ace-line ace-line old-record-id-OuphdyB66oaXaexoKD4lLtSvgnh\">Looking at the groups with higher birth rates, women aged 25-29 recorded approximately 140 births per 1,000 people in 1973, followed by the 20-25 age group at about 130 births, while the 30-35 group started at around 70 births. The 25-29 age group, despite maintaining the highest figures, showed a generally downward trend with some fluctuations, ending at about 120 births in 2008. The 20-25 age group saw a consistent decline to approximately 92 births, while in contrast, the 30-35 group demonstrated a steady increase, reaching roughly 88 births by the end of the period.</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>",
